pnpm -C driving_school_platform/nextjs_space check
```

Report the result.

## Required final report

At the end of each batch, report:

- files created/changed
- migrations created, if any
- dependencies added, if any
- endpoints changed, if any
- tests created/changed
- runtime behavior changed
- manual QA recommendations
- limitations
- confirmation that scope stayed within request
- **memory docs update needed: yes/no** — list files to update (or “none”) per memory maintenance policy

For **runtime / API / UI / sensitive** batches, final reports must also include the **Final Evidence Pack** and **Critical Claim Evidence Protocol** from `docs/ops/cursor-operating-model.md`:

- Run and paste `git status --short`, unstaged and staged diff stats/name lists, and validation output before claiming merge readiness.
- **Critical claims** (locks, tenant isolation, zero-write dry-run, all-or-nothing apply, no schema/auth/billing/demo/RLS changes, etc.) require **direct evidence** (paths, grep, diff snippet, or test reference) — not prose alone.
- If staged and unstaged changes differ, report **both** and explain the difference.
- Do **not** ask for merge readiness based only on a prose summary.
- If a generated patch is empty, stale, or omits untracked files, say so explicitly and regenerate evidence correctly (`git diff` vs `git diff --cached`; list `??` files separately).

For **runtime / API / UI / sensitive** batches, final reports must also include an **Implementation Conformance Matrix** (see `docs/ops/cursor-operating-model.md` — Implementation Conformance Matrix):

- Explicitly map **approved requirements** to actual implementation files, tests, and evidence.
- Explicitly identify any **deviations from the approved plan**.
- Do not hide deviations inside general prose; deviations must be called out in the matrix with status **CHANGED FROM PLAN** (or **PARTIAL / DEFERRED / NOT DONE**) and a short reason.
- If a **critical approved requirement** is **not implemented** or only **partially implemented**, Cursor must **stop** and ask for reviewer guidance (do not claim completion/merge readiness).

## Human-controlled merge (default workflow)

See `docs/ops/cursor-operating-model.md` — **Human-Controlled Merge Protocol** and `docs/ops/command-batteries.md` — Human-controlled close/merge battery.

- Do **not** run merge/push/branch-delete/archive commands by default.
- At batch close, provide Rui with the **manual close/merge command battery** (**Git Bash**, copy-paste-safe) instead of executing it.
- The battery must start with **`Assumed shell: Git Bash`** and use **one-line** Conventional Commit messages unless Rui explicitly needs otherwise.
- **Merge/push remains a human control point** — Rui merges when the batch is ready.
- If Rui **explicitly asks** Cursor to run merge/push (or commit/switch/pull/merge/branch-delete/archive), first **restate risks**, the **command plan**, and **working tree assumptions**; confirm before executing; still use Git Bash syntax unless Rui asked for PowerShell.

## Hard rules

- Do not commit secrets.
- Do not expose `passwordHash`, `tokenHash`, raw tokens, provider secrets, or raw provider errors.
- Do not trust `organizationId` from request body or query.
- Tenant scope must come from authenticated session and host guard.
- Dry-run endpoints must be **zero-write**.
- Apply/import endpoints must be **all-or-nothing** unless explicitly documented.
- No migrations unless explicitly requested.
- No production `migrate deploy` unless explicitly requested by the user.
- No new dependency without explicit justification.
- No demo sandbox quota/policy changes unless explicitly requested.
- No auth/email/rate-limit/RLS/security changes during unrelated UI/product batches.
- No broad cleanup/refactor inside feature batches.

## DAT domain rules

- **User** = login/account.
- **Student** = operational/academic record.
- Student can exist **without** User.
- `Student.userId` is **optional**.
- Student app access modes: `MANUAL_ONLY`, `INVITED`, `APP_USER`.
- `Lesson.studentId` = `Student.id`.
- Instructor has **User** and **Instructor** record.
- `Lesson.instructorId` = `Instructor.id`.
- API/UI may receive `instructorUserId` or `instructorEmail`; persistence must resolve to `Instructor.id`.
- `schoolStudentId` for A Conquistadora is **YY + NNN**, 5 digits.
- Importing students does **not** create Users, invitations, or emails.
- Invitation from Student record links future User to **existing** Student.
- Accepting invitation must **not** create duplicate Student.
- Practical lesson import creates **DRIVING COMPLETED IMPORT** lessons.
- Manual practical history creates **DRIVING COMPLETED MANUAL** lessons.
- Normal app-created lessons use **SYSTEM** source.

